.TH GEORGE-IPC 1 "October 2026" "George v3.0" "George Sovereign Manual"
.SH NAME
george-ipc \- Sovereign POSIX FIFO Async/Await, Flow Control, and Agentic IPC CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B george-ipc
.I command
[\fIarguments\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B george-ipc
is the primary command-line operator interface for the Sovereign POSIX FIFO Async/Await and Credit-Based Flow Control Protocol (v3).
It provides zero-daemon, pure-POSIX inter-process communication for subagents, autonomous workflows, and background task execution across the Blue Lodge architecture.
.PP
The protocol guarantees:
.IP \(bu 2
.B Kernel Write Atomicity:
Message frames are strictly bounded by \fBPIPE_BUF\fR (4096 bytes). Large payloads automatically spill over to disk and are transparently rehydrated upon receipt.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Credit-Based Flow Control:
Channels maintain a sliding token window. Writers consume credits; readers replenish credits, eliminating unbounded kernel buffer accumulation.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Request-Response Routing:
NDJSON frames contain unique RFC 4122 UUIDs, channel identifiers, and message types allowing multiplexed request-reply correlation.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Async Task Orchestration:
Background commands execute under promise manifests, supporting timeout-enforced barriers, monadic chaining, and clean process tree termination.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Autonomic Garbage Collection:
A single-pass GAWK supervisor automatically detects crashed keepers, cleans wedged queues, and prunes expired promise handles without external daemons.

.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS Channel Lifecycle
.TP
.B channel open \fIchannel_id\fR [\fIwindow_size\fR] [\fImax_idle\fR]
Creates a new structured IPC channel containing \fIdata.fifo\fR, \fIctrl.fifo\fR, \fIstate.json\fR, \fIstate.lock\fR, and \fIqueue/\fR.
Launches a synchronized background pipe keeper to retain file descriptors.
Default window size is 5; default max idle timeout is 300 seconds.
.TP
.B channel close \fIchannel_id\fR
Closes FIFOs, terminates the background keeper process tree, marks state as CLOSED, and reclaims all channel filesystem artifacts.
.TP
.B channel list
Outputs an aligned table of all active channels, their lifecycle status, window size, available credits, and backpressure flags.
.TP
.B channel status \fIchannel_id\fR
Displays full JSON state metadata for the specified channel, including sequence counters, keeper PID, and activity timestamps.
.TP
.B channel flush \fIchannel_id\fR
Non-blockingly drains unread messages from \fIdata.fifo\fR, clears buffered disk spillover, and resets credit tokens to the configured window.

.SS Flow Control & Backpressure
.TP
.B flow acquire \fIchannel_id\fR [\fItimeout\fR]
Acquires one transmission credit from the channel under atomic lock. If credits are exhausted or backpressure is asserted, polls until credits are granted or \fItimeout\fR (default 10s) expires.
.TP
.B flow grant \fIchannel_id\fR [\fIamount\fR]
Replenishes \fIamount\fR credits (default 1) in channel state and transmits a CREDIT wakeup ping across the control FIFO.
.TP
.B flow pause \fIchannel_id\fR
Asserts backpressure on the channel, blocking all subsequent credit acquisitions.
.TP
.B flow resume \fIchannel_id\fR
Clears backpressure on the channel, allowing producers to resume acquiring credits.
.TP
.B flow unstick \fIchannel_id\fR
Emergency recovery action: resets backpressure to false and restores credit tokens to the channel window size.

.SS Message Transmission & Reception
.TP
.B send \fIchannel_id\fR [\fItype\fR] [\fIpayload\fR] [\fIuuid\fR] [\fItimeout\fR]
Constructs an OKF-compliant NDJSON message frame, acquires transmission credit, assigns monotonic sequence numbers, and writes the frame atomically to \fIdata.fifo\fR.
If the payload exceeds 3800 bytes, transparent disk spillover is engaged.
.TP
.B recv \fIchannel_id\fR [\fItimeout\fR] [\fIfilter_type\fR] [\fIfilter_uuid\fR] [\fIauto_grant\fR]
Reads the next available frame from \fIdata.fifo\fR within \fItimeout\fR seconds.
Supports correlation filtering by message type and UUID. Rehydrates spilled payloads automatically and auto-grants replenishment credit.
.TP
.B write \fIchannel_id\fR \fIjson_frame\fR [\fItimeout\fR]
Backward-compatible wrapper for \fBsend\fR.
.TP
.B read \fIchannel_id\fR [\fItimeout\fR]
Backward-compatible wrapper for \fBrecv\fR.

.SS Asynchronous Tasks & Promises
.TP
.B async \fIchannel_id\fR \fIcommand\fR
Spawns \fIcommand\fR in the background, isolated from the terminal session. Writes an initial promise manifest and prints the resulting \fIpromise_id\fR.
.TP
.B await \fIpromise_id\fR [\fItimeout\fR]
Blocks until the async promise resolves (0) or rejects (non-zero). Outputs the command's stdout/stderr. On timeout (exit code 124), cleanly terminates the background process group.
.TP
.B await-all \fIp1,p2,p3...\fR [\fItimeout\fR]
Awaits concurrent barrier resolution for a comma-separated list of promise IDs. Fails fast if any promise rejects.
.TP
.B pipe \fIpromise_id\fR \fIchannel_id\fR \fIcommand_template\fR
Monadically chains completion of \fIpromise_id\fR into a successor command. The placeholder \fB{}\fR in \fIcommand_template\fR is replaced with the prior promise's output.
.TP
.B cancel \fIpromise_id\fR [\fIsignal\fR]
Cooperatively or forcefully terminates the worker process tree associated with \fIpromise_id\fR and marks the promise as CANCELED (exit code 125).
.TP
.B status \fItarget_id\fR
Displays JSON status for either a channel or an async promise manifest.

.SS Maintenance & Diagnostics
.TP
.B gc [\fI--dry-run\fR] [\fI--force\fR] [\fI--ttl <seconds>\fR]
Executes the GAWK protocol supervisor to audit all channels, keepers, and promises, cleaning dead processes and restoring wedged queues.
.TP
.B log [\fIlines\fR]
Displays the last \fIlines\fR (default 25) structured entries from \fI.george/ipc/ipc.log\fR.
.TP
.B config
Prints the active runtime tunables, including directory paths, credit windows, buffer limits, and timeouts.
.TP
.B version
Displays the george-ipc protocol version and build specification.

.SH MESSAGE FRAME SCHEMA (NDJSON)
Every message frame transmitted across the data pipe complies with the Google Open Knowledge Graph (OKF) envelope:
.PP
.nf
.RS
{
  "seq": 1,
  "type": "DATA",
  "channel": "subagent-alpha",
  "uuid": "7f2b1a8c-9e23-4d01-a1e4-8c9f201b5a2e",
  "sender_id": "george",
  "sender_role": "agent",
  "timestamp": 1790824644,
  "credits_granted": 0,
  "payload": { ... },
  "body": { ... }
}
.RE
.fi

.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
\fBIPC_OK\fR: Operation completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
\fBIPC_ERR_GENERIC\fR: Generic internal failure.
.TP
.B 2
\fBIPC_ERR_NOTFOUND\fR: Channel or promise not found (ENOENT).
.TP
.B 13
\fBIPC_ERR_PERMISSION\fR: Lock or permission denied (EACCES).
.TP
.B 16
\fBIPC_ERR_BUSY\fR: Resource contention or lock acquisition failure (EBUSY).
.TP
.B 22
\fBIPC_ERR_INVALID\fR: Invalid arguments or schema validation error (EINVAL).
.TP
.B 32
\fBIPC_ERR_PIPE\fR: Broken named pipe or channel aborted (EPIPE).
.TP
.B 110
\fBIPC_ERR_TIMEOUT\fR: Credit acquisition or flow control timed out (ETIMEDOUT).
.TP
.B 124
\fBIPC_ERR_AWAIT_TIMEOUT\fR: Promise await barrier timed out; worker process tree reaped.
.TP
.B 125
\fBIPC_ERR_CANCELED\fR: Task explicitly canceled via \fBcancel\fR.
.TP
.B 137
\fBIPC_ERR_CRASH\fR: Background process died prematurely or killed by signal (SIGKILL).

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FIFO_IPC_DIR
Root storage directory for channels, promises, and locks (default: \fI.george/ipc\fR).
.TP
.B FIFO_DEFAULT_WINDOW
Default credit allocation granted to new channels (default: 5).
.TP
.B FIFO_MAX_FRAME_BYTES
Maximum permissible raw frame size (default: 4096 bytes).
.TP
.B FIFO_POLL_INTERVAL
Polling sleep duration in flow control loops (default: 0.05 seconds).
.TP
.B FIFO_GC_MAX_IDLE
Idle threshold in seconds before a channel is marked stale (default: 300).
.TP
.B FIFO_GC_PROMISE_TTL
Retention duration in seconds for resolved promise outputs (default: 1800).

.SH FILES
.TP
.I .george/ipc/channels/<channel_id>/
Channel state directory containing \fIdata.fifo\fR, \fIctrl.fifo\fR, \fIstate.json\fR, \fIconfig.json\fR, and \fIqueue/\fR.
.TP
.I .george/ipc/promises/<promise_id>.json
Authoritative promise state manifest.
.TP
.I .george/ipc/promises/<promise_id>.out
Captured standard output and error stream from the async worker.
.TP
.I .george/ipc/payloads/<uuid>.payload
Transparent large-payload spillover files.
.TP
.I .george/ipc/ipc.log
High-speed append-only structured audit log.

